sangati avastha

  -- avastha: the state of a quantity at a specific point in a krama sequence
  -- initial-velocity and final-velocity are NOT different concepts
  -- they are the same concept (velocity) at purva-avastha and uttara-avastha
  -- avastha is more fundamental than physics — any ordered process has before/after states

  "krama-sthita sthiti-abheda"
  "purva-avastha-janya uttara-avastha-phala"
  "kramanusara-yukta"
  "svayambhu-yukta"

  -- purva-avastha: the state before a process / the initial condition
  -- uttara-avastha: the state after a process / the result condition
  -- svayambhu-yukta: states can chain — uttara of one process is purva of the next

shabda state-at-a-krama-point / the-condition-of-a-quantity-before-or-after-a-process-purva-is-initial-uttara-is-final

done
